WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.333
Why can a search for Acme's Q3 revenue miss the right chunk? Because a chunk split from its filing loses the company and the quarter.

2
00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:11.573
Contextual retrieval fixes that at indexing time,

3
00:00:11.573 --> 00:00:14.667
by having Claude explain each chunk using the full document.

4
00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:17.167
That explanation goes in front of the chunk,

5
00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:22.167
so embeddings and BM25 can find it by the company and the quarter.

6
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.087
In Anthropic's tests,

7
00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:27.227
that cut top-20 retrieval failure by 49%,

8
00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:30.233
but every chunk now costs more to index.

9
00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:32.853
So I'd check metadata first,

10
00:00:32.853 --> 00:00:37.453
and add the explanations only where a chunk still reads as anonymous.
